  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A philosopher named Jason Jorjani, drawing on the journalist Annie Jacobsen's book Area 51, about a secret US base in Nevada, says that test pilots of the U-2 and SR-71, high-flying American spy planes of the 1950s and 60s, were handed gorilla masks. According to the story, they were told that if they ever got close enough to a passenger airliner for its pilot to make eye contact, they should put the mask on first. Told this way, it suggests secret flights were made to look absurd so that any sighting would not be believed."
